WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.270
In March 2024, cocoa beans set a record.

2
00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:08.460
Cocoa futures in New York passed
10,000 dollars a metric ton,

3
00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:10.420
for the first time ever.

4
00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:13.270
Prices had roughly doubled since January.

5
00:00:13.270 --> 00:00:16.200
That is a loud signal to every grower:

6
00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:19.330
produce more. So when prices jump,

7
00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:22.120
why can some producers flood
the market while others

8
00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:24.230
cannot grow more for years?

9
00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:28.440
In this mission, you'll measure how
strongly supply responds to price,

10
00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:30.210
using a single number.

11
00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:32.580
Then you'll send the
same rise in demand into

12
00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:36.710
different markets and watch what
happens to price and output.

13
00:00:36.710 --> 00:00:40.200
Your mission: find out what
holds some producers back.
